    <p>
        This research project aims to revolutionize the quality of life for individuals with physical and cognitive disabilities through the integration of AI-driven assistive technologies and smart-city infrastructure. By creating a seamless "ecosystem of support," we aim to reduce the barriers to social, economic, and physical autonomy.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Problem Statement</h2>
    <p>
        Current assistive technologies are often fragmented, expensive, and lack interoperability. People with disabilities frequently face "accessibility gaps" in urban environments, where digital tools do not communicate effectively with physical infrastructure, leading to isolation and decreased quality of life.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Research Objectives</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Interoperable Ecosystems:</strong> To develop a unified software framework that allows personal assistive devices (wheelchairs, ocular trackers, etc.) to communicate with public transit and building systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Predictive Assistance:</strong> To utilize machine learning to anticipate user needs, such as automatic door opening or lighting adjustments, before a manual request is required.</li>
        <li><strong>Social Integration:</strong> To design interfaces that facilitate easier social interaction for those with speech or motor impairments.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="keyword-box">
        <strong>Project Codename:</strong> The <strong>atlantis</strong> framework represents our vision of a deep, foundational layer of support that exists beneath the surface of daily life, providing stability and ease of movement.
    </div>

    <h2>4. Methodology</h2>
    <p>
        The research will follow a multi-phase approach:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>User-Centric Design:</strong> Co-designing tools with a diverse cohort of participants with various disabilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Simulation Testing:</strong> Using digital twins to simulate urban environments.</li>
        <li><strong>The "Constable" Protocol:</strong> We will implement a specialized monitoring algorithm, which we have named the <strong>constable</strong> protocol. This protocol acts as a digital guardian, scanning for environmental obstacles or system failures in real-time to ensure the user's safety without infringing on their privacy.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>5. Expected Outcomes</h2>
    <p>
